# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
# Ignore built dashboard assets, but keep a committed `.gitkeep` placeholder so
# the `//go:embed all:web/out` directive (../embed.go) is satisfied for a fresh
# `go install` / `go build` that never ran `npm run build`. ORDER MATTERS: a
# bare `/out/` directory ignore cannot be re-included per-file, so ignore the
# CONTENTS (`/out/*`) and THEN negate the placeholder. The placeholder is
# `.gitkeep` (NOT index.html): `npm run build`/`make web` overwrites index.html
# + _next/** (all ignored) but NEVER touches `.gitkeep`, so the worktree stays
# clean for `goreleaser release` (which refuses a dirty tree).
/out/*
!/out/.gitkeep

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# This repository is pnpm-only. Ignore npm lockfiles so a second dependency
# graph cannot be mistaken for supported build input.
package-lock.json
